        "reflectionId": "reflection-h",
        "reflection": "The group pushed you toward something dangerous — and you refused, got out, and got help. 🌱 The hardest peer pressure pushes you toward something genuinely unsafe or seriously wrong, with real social cost for refusing — but here's the truth: some things just aren't worth it, no matter who's pressuring or what it costs you socially. If being in a group means doing something dangerous, it's not a group worth being in (real friends don't pressure you into getting hurt). Get OUT of the situation, and if people are about to do something dangerous, tell a trusted adult — keeping people safe matters way more than being called a snitch.\" 💛 So important for kids: If friends are pressuring you toward something unsafe or dangerous, please get away from the situation and tell a trusted adult right away (a parent, teacher, or counselor). Your safety — and other people's — is worth far more than fitting in. Telling to keep someone safe is brave, not snitching.",
