        "reflection": "That one was hard. Getting skipped in front of everyone is one of the most embarrassing feelings there is — and you didn't blow up or melt down. You waited, you asked her privately, and you found out the real story. 🌱\n\nTwo big lessons: ask before you assume (it's almost never as mean as it feels), and when you do speak up, do it privately and calmly — that protects you and the other person. And being fair even when you're hurt? That's the strongest thing a person can do.\n\nYou can't control every invitation. You can control your dignity — and yours was rock solid.",
