    "whyItMatters": "Here's a surprise: even best friends argue. Arguing doesn't mean a friendship is broken — it's totally normal. What actually matters is how you fix it. Solving an argument means staying calm instead of blowing up, listening to the other side, finding a fair solution, and not letting one small thing turn into a giant thing. The kids with the strongest friendships aren't the ones who never argue — they're the ones who know how to make up.",
