        "reflection": "That was the hardest kind of helping — because Jordan wasn't lonely from being bored, he was hurting. 🌱 You learned the deepest truth about showing up for someone: you don't need the perfect words, and you don't have to fix it. You just have to notice, sit with them, and let them know they're not alone. And when something's really big — like a hard situation at home — a good friend also points toward a trusted grown-up (a counselor, a teacher, a parent) who can truly help. You made someone feel seen on their worst day. That matters more than you know.\" 💛 Note for kids: If a friend is going through something really hard, or if you ever feel that way yourself, telling a trusted adult isn't betraying anyone — it's getting the right kind of help.",
