    "title": "Someone Breaks Your Trust",
    "skill": "Rebuilding trust (and knowing when to step back)",
    "whyItMatters": "When someone breaks your trust, it's confusing — should you forgive and trust them again, or protect yourself? Here's the secret most people never learn: trust and forgiveness are two different things. You can forgive someone (let go of the anger) AND still decide not to count on them the same way. A one-time mistake with a real sorry? Give another chance. The same letdown over and over, even after promises? It's okay to step back. Trust is earned back through actions, not words.",
