        "reflection": "That was the hardest one in the whole category — and you handled it like someone way older than you. 🌱 You gave Jordan real chances. You talked about it. And when the same thing kept happening anyway, you did the brave, grown-up thing: you forgave him (no hate, no revenge) and stepped back to protect yourself. Those aren't opposites. The deepest truth here: you can care about someone and still decide they're not someone you can fully count on. Protecting yourself from being hurt over and over isn't mean — it's self-respect. And putting your energy into the people who actually show up? That's how you end up surrounded by real friends.",
