        "reflectionId": "reflection-h",
        "reflection": "That was the hardest one in the whole category — because it wasn't just a game. You trained, you cared, and you still didn't make it. 🌱 And you handled it with incredible strength. You learned three huge things: it's okay — even important — to let yourself feel the disappointment. One 'no' is about one thing, not about your whole worth — don't let it spiral into 'I'm a failure.' And the bravest move of all is to feel it, learn from it, and try again. Everybody fails at things they care about. The ones who get great are the ones who get back up. That's you.\" 💛 Note for kids: When a disappointment feels really big or sticks around, talking to a trusted grown-up — a parent, a coach, a counselor — can really help. You don't have to carry the heavy stuff alone.",
