        "reflection": "The whole group misread Noor as 'stuck-up' — and you read her right. 🌱 Shyness is one of the most misread things there is: quiet kids get labeled snobby, rude, or 'too good for everyone,' when really they're just nervous. Reading people well means looking past the surface to what's really going on — and being willing to read someone differently than the crowd does. When you read a shy kid correctly, you can give them a fair chance and help others see them accurately. You might rescue a great, lonely friend from a misunderstanding.\" 💛 Note for kids: Lots of shy kids feel lonely because they get misjudged. Reaching out makes a huge difference. And if a shy or left-out kid seems really down or alone for a long time, letting a trusted adult or school counselor know is a kind thing to do.",
