        "reflection": "You're the quiet one in a world that acts like louder is better — and you learned to value who you are. 🌱 Hear this: there is nothing wrong with being quiet. Louder isn't better, just different — and quiet people bring listening, thoughtfulness, and depth the world needs. Don't force yourself to be someone you're not (it's exhausting and fake). But quiet doesn't mean voiceless — speak up when it really matters, on your terms. Quiet and confident, not quiet and invisible. And find the people who appreciate the real, quiet you.\" 💛 Note for kids: Being quiet or introverted is completely okay — it's a personality, not a problem. If people make you feel 'wrong' for it and that starts to weigh on you, talking to a parent, counselor, or trusted grown-up can really help. You don't need to be loud to matter.",
