        "reflectionId": "reflection-h",
        "reflection": "Meanness had become real bullying — and you took it seriously and got help. 🌱 Sometimes meanness escalates into bullying — targeted, ongoing, cruel — and then 'don't take it personally, just ignore it' isn't enough. Recognize when mean has become bullying, take it seriously, and GET A TRUSTED ADULT (telling about bullying is brave and smart, not weak or tattling). Guard your self-image fiercely — never let repeated cruelty make you believe the mean things (a lie repeated is still a lie). And even though mean people are often hurting inside, that is NEVER your fault or your job to fix. Protect yourself, and let grown-ups help.\" 💛 Important for kids: If someone is bullying you — being cruel to you on purpose, over and over — please tell a trusted adult (a parent, teacher, or counselor) right away. It is not weak or tattling; it's the brave, smart thing. You don't have to face it alone, and you never have to believe a single cruel word they say about you.",
        "saveLine": "When mean becomes bullying, getting help is the strong move — and I'll never believe what cruel people say about me."
