        "reflection": "You'd disappeared into the group — and you found your own voice again. 🌱 Some people follow so much they lose their voice, going along with everything until they don't even know what THEY think, want, or like. Reclaim it: it's okay to have your own opinions, to like different things, to disagree sometimes — a good friend group has room for the real YOU. And your voice matters most in the moment the group pressures you toward something you don't want or that isn't right. You're always allowed to say no, even to your friends — and a trusted adult is there if the pressure ever gets serious.\" 💛 Important for kids: You're always allowed to say no — even to your friends — especially about anything that feels unsafe or wrong. If a group ever pressures you toward something dangerous and won't let up, please tell a trusted adult. Your voice and your choices matter.",
