        "reflectionId": "reflection-h",
        "reflection": "Grace was in real pain — and you helped most by not trying to fix it. 🌱 The hardest listening is when someone's hurting and every instinct says solve it, cheer them up, give advice. But often people don't need solutions — they need to feel heard. So: resist the urge to fix or minimize ('it's not a big deal'), validate the feeling, and ask what they need instead of assuming. 'I'm here' helps more than any advice. And when the pain is really big, being present and gently pointing them toward a trusted grown-up is the kindest combo of all.\" 💛 Note for kids: Sitting with a hurting friend is a wonderful thing to do. When their pain feels really big or lasts a long time, helping them reach a trusted adult — a parent, counselor, or coach — is part of being a great friend.",
