        "reflectionId": "reflection-h",
        "reflection": "The worry got big and wouldn't quiet — and you were gentle with yourself and reached for help. 🌱 Sometimes nervousness becomes BIG — persistent worry or anxiety that won't quiet down, that's overwhelming, maybe affecting your sleep or your days. First: feeling it doesn't make you broken or weak — lots of people feel this, it's not a flaw. Be gentle with yourself, and lean on small steady healthy tools (slow breathing, talking it out, routine, calming activities). And this is important — overwhelming or persistent anxiety is something a trusted adult (a parent, counselor, or doctor) can really help with. Telling them isn't weak; it's the smart, brave thing, and you don't have to carry big worry alone.\" 💛 So important for kids: If worry or anxiety feels overwhelming, sticks around, or is affecting your sleep, your days, or how you feel — please talk to a parent, counselor, or trusted adult. There's real help out there, feeling anxious is never a flaw or your fault, and you deserve support.",
